Self-training

Firstly, we can get model predictions via running:

python train_net.py --num-gpus 1 --config-file model_zoo/configs/CutLER-CraterDataset/cascade_mask_rcnn_R_50_FPN_modified.yaml --test-dataset crater_dataset_train --eval-only TEST.DETECTIONS_PER_IMAGE 30 MODEL.WEIGHTS output0/model_final.pth OUTPUT_DIR output1/ 

Secondly, we can run the following command to generate the json file for the first round of self-training:
  
python tools/get_self_training_ann.py --new-pred output1/inference/coco_instances_results.json --prev-ann /home/isradmin/Desktop/CutLER/CutLER/datasets/crater_dataset/annotations/train.json --save-path /home/isradmin/Desktop/CutLER/CutLER/datasets/crater_dataset/annotations/train_r1.json --threshold 0.7
  
Finally, place "train_r1.json" under "/home/isradmin/Desktop/CutLER/CutLER/datasets/crater_dataset/annotations", then launch the self-training process:
  
python train_net.py --num-gpus 1 --config-file model_zoo/configs/CutLER-CraterDataset/cascade_mask_rcnn_R_50_FPN_self_train_modified.yaml --train-dataset crater_dataset_train_r1 MODEL.WEIGHTS output/model_final.pth OUTPUT_DIR output/self-train-r1/
  
Na pasta do output, para ver métricas, escrever no terminal:

tensorboard --logdir .

